Plain Vue vs Nuxt
The 2026 debate: learn via Nuxt directly (like Next.js for React) vs plain Vue first. Research conclusion: plain Vue first — the patterns (composables, router, pinia) are 100% transferable; Nuxt adds conventions SSR. Move to Nuxt when you need: SEO, SSR, your own API routes.

Nuxt Conventions (file-based)
 = automatic routing (pages/about.vue → /about),  = page templates,  = auto-import (no manual imports),  = root. Our Vue project structure is already 80% similar — intentionally.

useFetch / useAsyncData
Nuxt wraps fetching with caching, deduplication, and SSR-aware state: . The useFetch you wrote in lesson 14 is its miniature version.

Server Routes
Nuxt can host its own API:  → . Frontend backend in one codebase (Nitro). This is the main reason to switch to Nuxt.

